That...

153
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:47,250
That could work!

154
00:06:50,970 --> 00:06:53,890
Sleep Pipe

155
00:06:59,780 --> 00:07:02,600
I look... I look so cool!

156
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:04,470
I'm already a total rocker chick!

157
00:07:04,470 --> 00:07:06,590
I look like a real somebody!

158
00:07:06,590 --> 00:07:08,030
The people can't look away!

159
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:14,160
Someone's just gotta talk to me now!

160
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:18,230
I'm gonna be all over this
year's culture festival!

161
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,180
So you could see the corgi's butt...

162
00:07:35,300 --> 00:07:36,520
Do we move rooms next period?

163
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:37,310
Science Room B.

164
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:39,560
Hey, wanna karaoke after this?

165
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,610
Great idea!

166
00:07:40,610 --> 00:07:41,600
You sure?

167
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,500
Wonder what I should sing...

168
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,570
Huh?

169
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:54,340
Did I go overboard
hyping myself up last night?

170
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:57,750
But I'm putting out such
powerful rocker chick vibes...

171
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:00,830
D-Did I end up making myself unapproachable?!

172
00:08:00,830 --> 00:08:01,720
No, no, no!

173
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:03,210
I'm having a mental breakdown!

174
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:04,710
Wow, look at that!

175
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:04,580
Thump

176
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:05,340
At what?

177
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:08,040
I-If they're laughing at me now,
it won't just be a mental breakdown,

178
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,710
it'll be mental annihilation!

179
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,920
Aw, it's so cute, I've gotta laugh!

180
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,390
Guitar?

181
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,940
My day's immediately better!

182
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,520
Right, Kita-chan?

183
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,020
Kita-chan?

184
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:21,100
Sorry, sorry! What was it?

185
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,030
Look, I know.

186
00:08:27,030 --> 00:08:30,280
You can't put the onus on others
and expect perfect results.

187
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:37,760
This is a gathering place for
people just as lonely as me.

188
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:40,090
I bet that guy's separated from—

189
00:08:39,030 --> 00:08:40,090
Papa!

190
00:08:41,910 --> 00:08:43,710
Sorry we're late!

191
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:44,870
Hey, no problem.

192
00:08:44,870 --> 00:08:45,800
Now, let's grab dinner!

193
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,140
What would you like?

194
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:48,140
They're the perfect freakin' family!

195
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:51,460
Please forgive my presumptuous empathizing...

196
00:08:53,490 --> 00:08:56,420
Ah. I broke 30,000 subscribers.

197
00:08:57,360 --> 00:08:59,440
Hey, that's right.

198
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,720
The online world is where I belong.

199
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:05,360
Sorta makes me not wanna go back to school...

200
00:09:07,490 --> 00:09:09,220
Guitar!

201
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:13,710
That's a guitar, right?

202
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:14,770
Do you play?!

203
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:18,270
Hello?

204
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:21,200
I-I haven't talked to anyone
in so long... my voice!

205
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:23,420
Hey, sorry to ambush you.

206
00:09:23,420 --> 00:09:26,500
I'm Nijika Ijichi, second-year
at Shimo-Kitazawa High.

207
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,450
Hitori Goto. Shuka High. First-year.

208
00:09:30,450 --> 00:09:31,830
So tell me, Hitori-chan...

209
00:09:31,830 --> 00:09:33,170
Right to first names, are we?!

210
00:09:33,170 --> 00:09:35,230
How good are you at guitar?

211
00:09:35,730 --> 00:09:37,220
Pretty decent, I guess...

212
00:09:37,220 --> 00:09:38,590
Really?!

213
00:09:38,590 --> 00:09:41,290
Say, I'm in kind of a fix here...

214
00:09:41,290 --> 00:09:43,180
If you can't do it, that's okay, but...

215
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:45,250
It's really okay, but I'm in a real fix...

216
00:09:45,250 --> 00:09:47,190
There's nothing okay about her!

217
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,560
Okay, I'll come right out with it!

218
00:09:50,180 --> 00:09:55,440
Please, will you play second
guitar for my band for today?!

219
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,360
Band?

220
00:09:57,360 --> 00:10:01,180
We've got a concert coming up,
and our guitarist just split!

221
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:04,110
The song's not too hard!
You'll pick it up right away!

222
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:04,110
A concert?! Right now?!

223
00:10:04,110 --> 00:10:05,730
Please! Please!

224
00:10:06,070 --> 00:10:06,950
Um, err...

225
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:13,270
Thanks! Let's head to the club!

226
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:15,230
I haven't even said anything yet!

227
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:19,840
I got dragged along.

228
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:22,440
Do you come to Shimo-Kita a lot, Hitori-chan?

229
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,720
Oh, well...

230
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:27,310
Right, like I've got the courage to visit
a fashion town for trendy people...

231
00:10:27,810 --> 00:10:29,780
We're almost to the club.

232
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,870
Nijika-chan's fashionable, too.

233
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:36,400
She's got the real rocker-chick vibe.

234
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,880
Meanwhile, I'm in a potato-quality tracksuit

235
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,230
with a real bear of a set of bags under my
eyes, and a back as arched as a cat...

236
00:10:41,230 --> 00:10:43,780
Wait, do I also smell like mold?

237
00:10:43,780 --> 00:10:45,700
I spend so much time in the closet...

238
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:47,370
No, I smell like mothballs.

239
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:52,130
Meanwhile, Nijika-chan smells great!

240
00:10:52,130 --> 00:10:55,380
She smells just the way
a high school girl should!

241
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:56,980
Oh, am I walking too fast?

242
00:10:56,980 --> 00:10:57,800
N-No...

243
00:10:58,170 --> 00:11:02,040
The club we're gonna play at
is called Starry.

244
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,680
My big sister's the manager there.

245
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:04,680
Playing at a club...

246
00:11:04,970 --> 00:11:07,180
That sounds weirdly legit.

247
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:09,060
Wait, what's my heart doing?

248
00:11:09,350 --> 00:11:10,240
And so...

249
00:11:11,450 --> 00:11:13,770
I've been working there part-time...

250
00:11:16,010 --> 00:11:19,070
Hitori-chan, are you
actually pretty athletic?

251
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:24,170
N-No, but I'm always the last one standing
in dodgeball for some reason.

252
00:11:24,170 --> 00:11:25,700
I... I see.

253
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:28,620
Me? Playing in a club?

254
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:32,040
No, don't back down now!

255
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:35,290
Remember your daydreams of
performing at the culture festival!

256
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:40,320
And your first solo show at Zepp Super Arena!

257
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:43,110
Hitori! Hitori! Hitori!

258
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:46,710
I'm the girl who sold out the Budokan...

259
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:47,600
What?

260
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,720
Oh, nothing!

261
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:53,510
Please, don't let her think she
made a mistake choosing me!

262
00:11:53,510 --> 00:11:55,440
I might've made a mistake choosing her...

263
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:57,240
We're here!

264
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,230
This is the place!

265
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:02,570
Th-The dark lands?

266
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:05,400
Good morning!

267
00:12:08,210 --> 00:12:10,120
My first club...

268
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:13,870
It's so dark... So stuffy...

269
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:15,960
I-It's so soothing!

270
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,500
You okay, Hitori-chan?

271
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,020
I'm home!

272
00:12:19,020 --> 00:12:19,880
It is not!

273
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:22,130
Could we ask the PA to record again?

274
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,510
That's the band that's playing today.

275
00:12:22,130 --> 00:12:25,250
I thought bands would be intimidating,

276
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:25,270
They might be a little older than us?

277
00:12:25,250 --> 00:12:28,850
but they're all indoorsy, shy introverts!

278
00:12:25,270 --> 00:12:27,880
After they're done, we'll rehearse too.

279
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:30,150
They're just like me!

280
00:12:30,150 --> 00:12:31,980
That there's the PA.

281
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:34,560
No drinks on the equipment!

282
00:12:33,140 --> 00:12:34,560
Good morning.

283
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,620
Please forgive my arrogance!

284
00:12:36,620 --> 00:12:37,520
What's wrong now?!

285
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:39,740
You're finally back.

286
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:40,530
Ryo!

287
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,520
This is Hitori Goto. Hitori-chan!

288
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:46,240
I met her in the park by miraculous
happenstance! She's a guitarist!

289
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,390
Oh?

290
00:12:47,390 --> 00:12:49,530
Scary! Is she glaring at me?

291
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,870
This is Ryo Yamada. She plays bass.

292
00:12:51,870 --> 00:12:54,900
I-I'm Hitori Goto! I'm so very sorry!

293
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:55,750
Hang on!

294
00:12:56,170 --> 00:12:57,590
Y-You're okay!

295
00:12:57,590 --> 00:12:59,760
Ryo's just not the expressive type.

296
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:01,670
Feel free to call her weird! She likes it!

297
00:13:01,670 --> 00:13:03,280
I don't, actually.

298
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,380
Seemed like she did...

299
00:13:04,670 --> 00:13:06,740
By the way, about the manager...

300
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:08,980
She told you to practice until it was time,

301
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:11,820
but instead you snuck out of the club,

302
00:13:11,820 --> 00:13:13,360
so she got so mad she went out shopping.

303
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:14,230
N-No way!

304
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:16,690
Let's be in the studio before she comes back!

305
00:13:17,090 --> 00:13:18,310
You too, Hitori-chan!

306
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,210
C'mon!

307
00:13:20,650 --> 00:13:21,780
R-Right!

308
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,780
Real life is scary.

309
00:13:24,660 --> 00:13:29,570
But I feel like there's
some fun stuff coming up!

310
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:33,120
Here's today's set list and score.

311
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:36,160
Wh-Where are the other band members?

312
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,820
This is everyone!

313
00:13:37,820 --> 00:13:40,000
We'll be doing all instrumentals this time.

314
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:43,660
Right. I can handle this song.

315
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:46,510
Though without any vocals, the playing's
gotta be all that much better...

316
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,400
But I'm supposedly good at guitar. I can do this.

317
00:13:49,400 --> 00:13:50,720
I think I can do this!

318
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:54,340
Gorilla?

319
00:13:57,230 --> 00:14:00,190
Maybe they'll be blown away by my playing!

320
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:04,570
I mean, I get pretty good...
pretty decent reactions online.

321
00:14:01,620 --> 00:14:02,860
Let's take it right from the top.

322
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:06,580
It's your first time,
so we'll run through slow,

323
00:14:05,050 --> 00:14:07,730
I even have 30,000 subscribers!

324
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:09,030
then we can speed it up
as you get used to it.

325
00:14:07,730 --> 00:14:09,840
Yeah, let's do this!

326
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:11,080
Okay, let's go!

327
00:14:26,630 --> 00:14:27,840
You suck!

328
00:14:29,090 --> 00:14:30,650
H-How can I suck?

329
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:31,790
Ah, I'm kidding!

330
00:14:30,650 --> 00:14:32,730
I'm guitarhero!

331
00:14:31,790 --> 00:14:34,890
Well, not totally kidding, but...
Ah, I'm sorry!

332
00:14:32,730 --> 00:14:34,890
I've got 30,000 subscribers!

333
00:14:34,890 --> 00:14:36,470
Allow me to explain!

334
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:46,230
Guitar Man's
Easy-to-Learn
Hitori Classes

335
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:41,130
In a band, it's super important to be in
sync with your fellow live performers!

336
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,940
But Hitori has social anxiety
and can't make eye contact,

337
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:45,670
and she'll be inclined to
rush ahead of the others!

338
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,030
She might be an awesome solo player,

339
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,740
God

340
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,740
Social Butterfly

341
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,740
Normal Person

342
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,740
Water Flea

343
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:51,740
Hitori

344
00:14:48,030 --> 00:14:51,740
but when in a band, she's sub-water-flea
level, the worst there is!

345
00:14:52,010 --> 00:14:54,280
Hello. I'm Plankton Goto.

346
00:14:54,280 --> 00:14:57,080
She sounds like an unfunny comedian!

347
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,710
And thus, Hitori Goto turned to dust,

348
00:14:59,710 --> 00:15:02,960
and never picked up a guitar again.

349
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:05,630
BOCCHI THE ROCK!

350
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:05,630
THE END

351
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:11,010
Water Flea Hitori Goto

352
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:11,010
Drummer Nijika Ijichi

353
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:11,010
Bassist Ryo Yamada

354
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:11,010
Guitar Man As Himself

355
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:11,010
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

356
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:12,760
Come out, please!

357
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,600
The show's about to start!

358
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,520
I c-c-can't do it!

359
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:19,180
It's not your fault!
We just came together today!

360
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,440
It's not like I'm very good either.

361
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,770
I'm very good.

362
00:15:24,230 --> 00:15:26,360
Just look at me, okay!

363
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:28,140
Stay here in reality!

364
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:32,680
It isn't like I could
do the intro or anything...

365
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:36,570
I-I could offer up my life
to put on a harakiri show!

366
00:15:36,570 --> 00:15:39,490
Th-They'll at least remember
the name of the band, right?

367
00:15:39,490 --> 00:15:40,880
Sorry I sucked!

368
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,920
That's a little too rock!

369
00:15:42,300 --> 00:15:43,450
It's okay.

370
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:47,130
If they boo you, I'll give
them a bonk with my bass.

371
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,130
Bonk.

372
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:50,680
Does a bass make such a fancy noise?

373
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,720
I mean, bloodshed is pretty rock.

374
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:53,630
It's rock.

375
00:15:53,630 --> 00:15:55,730
You can't justify everything with "rock"!

376
00:15:55,730 --> 00:16:00,170
Besides, it'll probably just be my
friends who come to watch us play!

377
00:16:00,990 --> 00:16:03,630
And Nijika is my only friend, so...

378
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:07,720
Normal high school girls
don't know good music from bad.

379
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:10,030
That kind of take could get you
in trouble on the internet.

380
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:12,730
Okay? So just chill!

381
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,760
I d-dunno...

382
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:16,550
I know good music from bad.

383
00:16:16,550 --> 00:16:18,170
Well, you're not normal.

384
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:21,540
Hey, that wasn't a compliment.

385
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,140
Sorry.

386
00:16:23,590 --> 00:16:24,720
But...

387
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,460
We can't force her.

388
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:29,060
You're right.

389
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:30,700
Sorry to push you so hard.

390
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:32,170
No, actually...

391
00:16:32,970 --> 00:16:37,050
I r-really was happy you reached out to me.

392
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:40,600
I've wanted to be in a band for so long...

393
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,470
B-But I couldn't get the people together...

394
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:46,520
So I just upload covers
to the internet instead.

395
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:48,190
What do you usually play?

396
00:16:48,190 --> 00:16:51,230
M-Mostly songs by popular bands
from the last few years,

397
00:16:51,230 --> 00:16:54,260
so I could play them right away
once the band got together...

398
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:54,990
That's awesome!

399
00:16:55,280 --> 00:16:56,800
It's not.

400
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:59,380
It's the reason I'm the way I am now.

401
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:02,750
Being in a band with other people
was a pipe dream after all.

402
00:17:03,130 --> 00:17:05,360
Covering all popular songs?

403
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:07,730
She sounds like guitarhero-san!

404
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:08,460
Have you heard of her?

405
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:11,630
She's probably about our age, I think...

406
00:17:09,210 --> 00:17:11,170
guitarhero...

407
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:18,300
[Guitar] Acid "Spring Snow" [Gave it a try]

408
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:18,300
Views: 1,012

409
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:18,300
Sorry I can't upload very often nowadays!
There's just so much going on at high school!
Next time I'll try a song I do all the time
with my friends at karaoke!

410
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:18,300
10 comments Sort

411
00:17:11,630 --> 00:17:12,990
M-Me?!

412
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:15,560
I'll send you a link if you haven't!

413
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:18,160
She's super awesome! You should hear her!

414
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,080
Awe... some?

415
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:23,750
She comes up in my recommendations
a lot, so I've seen her too.

416
00:17:23,750 --> 00:17:25,140
She really is excellent.

417
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:26,040
Right?!

418
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,940
Though her naming sense is a bit cringy...

419
00:17:28,690 --> 00:17:29,650
It is?!

420
00:17:29,650 --> 00:17:33,520
I follow her with notifications on!

421
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:35,780
I'd love to play with her some day!

422
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:37,660
You just did, actually...

423
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:41,280
Look, what I'm getting at here

424
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:44,770
is that even awesome, popular people
are out there playing guitar,

425
00:17:44,770 --> 00:17:48,580
lots and lots of them,
in places we're not even watching.

426
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,840
You should watch her later!

427
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:52,950
I think you'll get what I mean
if you watch the videos.

428
00:17:54,650 --> 00:18:00,010
I always figured real-life people
didn't care about me at all...

429
00:18:02,470 --> 00:18:05,940
You can't give up on playing in a band
just because it didn't work out today!

430
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:08,290
It's possible it's our problem, anyway...

431
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:09,000
Our problem?

432
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:11,090
Hitori-chan?

433
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:14,780
But someone this nice has been
watching me all this time,

434
00:18:14,780 --> 00:18:17,170
and actually spoke to me...

435
00:18:17,170 --> 00:18:18,240
She stood up.

436
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:22,160
It's the kind of miracle
most people never experience!

437
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:24,820
I can't let it go to waste!

438
00:18:25,610 --> 00:18:27,500
I... I'm...

439
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:30,920
D-Do you want to perform after all?

440
00:18:33,330 --> 00:18:34,420
Hitori-chan?

441
00:18:34,420 --> 00:18:36,320
I know all that, rationally...

442
00:18:36,320 --> 00:18:37,820
But I'm still too scared...

443
00:18:37,820 --> 00:18:40,390
There's no way I can play
in front of an audience...

444
00:18:40,640 --> 00:18:43,330
If you're scared,
you could play from in here.

445
00:18:40,930 --> 00:18:44,310
Ripe Mangos

446
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:48,560
Ripe Mangos

447
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:48,560
I-It's the same environment
that I play in all the time!

448
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:51,190
Where exactly do you live?

449
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:56,150
Ripe Mangos

450
00:18:51,630 --> 00:18:54,640
How you feelin' tonight, Shimo-Kita?!

451
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,150
She's suddenly more outgoing.

452
00:18:56,430 --> 00:18:59,480
By the way, how do you
want us to introduce you?

453
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:02,170
"Hitori-chan"? Should we use your real name?

454
00:19:02,170 --> 00:19:03,900
I'd... I'd rather not...

455
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:05,770
Any nicknames, then?

456
00:19:05,770 --> 00:19:09,020
In middle school, they called me
"Hey" and "You there"...

457
00:19:09,020 --> 00:19:10,840
I don't think those are nicknames!

458
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:14,790
I never knew anyone well enough
to get nicknames from them!

459
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,220
Hitori...

460
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,940
Hitoribocchi (all alone)...

461
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:19,120
How about Bocchi-chan?

462
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,180
Another tactless comment!

463
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:23,290
I'm B-B-Bocchi!

464
00:19:23,290 --> 00:19:24,140
She likes it?

465
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,180
It's just my first ever nickname...

466
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,360
This is making me teary-eyed.

467
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:31,030
Oh, you haven't told me your band name yet.

468
00:19:33,110 --> 00:19:34,630
It's Kessoku Band.

469
00:19:37,030 --> 00:19:39,020
Kessoku Band...

470
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,820
Isn't that the word for "zip tie"?

471
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:42,570
It's brilliant.

472
00:19:42,570 --> 00:19:44,820
It's the worst pun!
We're totally changing it!

473
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:46,600
Why? It's cute.

474
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:47,810
Y-Yes.

475
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:52,050
Band name aside, it's time to play!

476
00:19:53,190 --> 00:19:54,420
Don't worry.

477
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:58,550
The key is to have fun, even if you suck!

478
00:19:58,550 --> 00:20:01,260
Your feelings really come
out in your playing, see?

479
00:20:01,980 --> 00:20:03,680
R-Right...

480
00:20:03,920 --> 00:20:07,040
We can always work on the
skill part next time.

481
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:07,720
Yeah.

482
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:09,540
Next... time...

483
00:20:09,540 --> 00:20:10,780
Okay, let's go!

484
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:11,380
Right.

485
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:15,690
They're okay with there being a next time!

486
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:22,240
Nice to meet you! We're Kessoku Band!

487
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:25,260
We'll play a bunch of
songs you probably know,

488
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,320
so please enjoy!

489
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:27,700
Who's that?

490
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:41,560
I hate that I can't play as
well as I usually do, but...

491
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:46,390
playing in a band with other
people is so much fun!

492
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:52,100
I've never really shone before today...

493
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:53,730
And I still don't!

494
00:20:53,730 --> 00:20:57,030
This might actually be a low point for me!

495
00:21:01,030 --> 00:21:02,880
Boy, I screwed up!

496
00:21:02,880 --> 00:21:04,800
Your intro bombed, too.

497
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:05,820
E-Excuse me!

498
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:07,530
B-B-B...

499
00:21:07,530 --> 00:21:08,390
What?

500
00:21:08,390 --> 00:21:10,110
B-B-B-B-B...

501
00:21:10,110 --> 00:21:11,730
Okay, you're freaking me out!

502
00:21:12,250 --> 00:21:17,010
B-Before our next performance, I'm gonna get
brave enough to say hello to my classmates!

503
00:21:17,010 --> 00:21:18,170
What a dramatic declaration.

504
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:20,250
Such growth...

505
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:21,600
Okay, I get it.

506
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:22,320
Sure!

507
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:26,550
Then let's have a Bocchi-chan-welcome-party-
slash-concert-post-mortem!

508
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:30,260
Actually, I'm pretty exhausted from
all this social interaction, so I'm gonna go.

509
00:21:30,630 --> 00:21:31,850
Sorry. I'm sleepy.

510
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:33,760
P-Pardon me!

511
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:41,220
There's no "ties" in this band at all!

512
00:21:49,370 --> 00:21:51,300
I'm gonna get over my social anxiety

513
00:21:51,300 --> 00:21:54,730
and bring out my full guitarhero powers!

514
00:21:56,890 --> 00:21:57,990
For Nijika-chan,

515
00:21:57,990 --> 00:21:59,250
Ryo-san,

516
00:21:59,250 --> 00:22:01,210
and Kessoku Band!

517
00:22:02,860 --> 00:22:04,960
S-Sorry! Sorry!

518
00:23:34,970 --> 00:23:39,980
#02 See You Tomorrow

519
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,750
Watch it!
